<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- A WebView takes the prefers-color-scheme its page sees from the app
         theme's isLightTheme attribute and never from the device's night
         setting - so under a theme that is dark whatever the device is doing,
         which @android:style/Theme.Material is, style.css's default scheme and
         the drawer's "Follow the system" have no system to follow: the page is
         dark on a phone in light mode, and only the drawer can get it back.
         One name over the two platform themes is what puts that back - the
         light one here, the dark one in values-night - and the activity picks up
         whichever the device is set to when it is created. (Only then: uiMode is
         one of its configChanges, see the manifest, so a night switch while the
         app is open is not a restart and may not reach the page. The band round
         the cutout follows the page itself, so it cannot disagree either way.)

         Nothing else is styled, there being nothing native on screen to style -
         the UI is a WebView, and a Toast and the file chooser are all that ever
         appears over it - except the window itself, which is the page's header
         colour so that a cold start is not a flash of white before the page.

         And the system bars, which are on screen (the app is edge-to-edge, not
         fullscreen) but transparent, so that what shows through them is the
         page's own colour - see paint() in MainActivity, which draws that band
         and asks for icons legible against it. Transparent is the app's to ask
         for only up to API 34: from 35 a window that targets it is edge-to-edge
         whatever it says and these two colours are ignored, the bars being
         transparent there by default. windowLightStatusBar is the same request
         paint() makes, for the moment before it can be made in code: it is what
         the band a cold start puts up needs, and is the one item of these that
         differs between the pair. -->
    <style name="Theme.Webshark" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/band</item>
        <item name="android:windowDrawsSystemBarBackgrounds">true</item>
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <!-- ...and neither is scrimmed on the app's behalf, the band being a
             colour the bars' icons are already picked to be legible on. -->
        <item name="android:enforceStatusBarContrast">false</item>
        <item name="android:enforceNavigationBarContrast">false</item>
        <!-- dark icons, on the light scheme's head colour -->
        <item name="android:windowLightStatusBar">true</item>
        <item name="android:windowLightNavigationBar">true</item>
    </style>
</resources>
